(1. Executive Summary) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.078 g
40. 609. Td
(This document provides a detailed explanation of PHP's `$_GET` and `$_POST` superglobal variables, which) Tj
T* (are fundamental for handling data submitted via HTTP requests, typically from HTML forms. We will explore) Tj
T* (their core definitions, how they differ in terms of data transmission and visibility, their respective use cases,) Tj
T* (and important security considerations. Understanding these superglobals is crucial for any PHP developer) Tj
T* (building interactive web applications that collect user input.) Tj
ET
