(Security Implications of choosing GET:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.078 g
40. 723. Td
( If GET were used, the username, email, and especially the password would be visible directly in the) Tj
T* (browser's URL bar, in browser history, and in server logs. This makes the sensitive information easily) Tj
T* (accessible to anyone looking over the user's shoulder, or if the URL is accidentally shared or logged, leading) Tj
T* (to severe security vulnerabilities. POST hides this data in the request body, making it much more secure for) Tj
T* (sensitive information.) Tj
